Article 3 Where an administrative organ or its functionary, in exercising its/his administrative functions and powers, commits any of the following acts infringing upon the personal rights of a citizen, the victim shall have the right to obtain compensation:
(1) illegally detaining a citizen or illegally taking administrative compulsory measures restricting the personal freedom of a citizen;
(2) unlawfully taking a citizen into custody or unlawfully depriving a citizen of his personal freedom by other means;
(3) causing physical injury or death to a citizen by beating, maltreating or other acts, or by instigating or conniving at such acts by others;
(4) illegally using weapons or police instruments to cause physical injury or death to a citizen; or
(5) other illegal acts causing physical injury or death to a citizen.

Article 4 Where an administrative organ or its functionary, in exercising its/his administrative functions and powers, commits any of the following acts infringing upon the property rights of a citizen, legal person or other organization, the victim shall have the right to obtain compensation:
(1) illegally imposing an administrative penalty such as a fine, revocation of a permit or license, order to suspend production or business operation, or confiscation of property;
(2) illegally taking administrative compulsory measures such as sealing up, seizing or freezing property;
(3) illegally requisitioning or expropriating property; or
(4) other illegal acts causing damage to property.

Article 17 Where an organ exercising functions and powers of investigation, prosecution and adjudication, or a detention house, prison administration authority, or a functionary thereof, in exercising its/his functions and powers, commits any of the following acts infringing upon the personal rights of a citizen, the victim shall have the right to obtain compensation:
(1) taking a detention measure against a citizen in violation of the provisions of the Criminal Procedure Law, or taking a detention measure against a citizen in accordance with the conditions and procedures of the Criminal Procedure Law but the period of detention exceeds the time limit specified by the Criminal Procedure Law, and later a decision is made to dismiss the case, not to prosecute, or a judgment of not guilty is rendered, terminating the investigation of criminal liability;
(2) after taking an arrest measure against a citizen, a decision is made to dismiss the case, not to prosecute, or a judgment of not guilty is rendered, terminating the investigation of criminal liability;
(3) a retrial in accordance with the procedure for adjudication supervision changes the original judgment to a judgment of not guilty, and the original sentence has already been executed;
(4) extorting a confession by torture, or causing physical injury or death to a citizen by beating, maltreating or other acts, or by instigating or conniving at such acts by others; or
(5) illegally using weapons or police instruments to cause physical injury or death to a citizen.

Article 19 The State shall not bear compensation liability in any of the following circumstances:
(1) a person is placed in custody or sentenced to a criminal penalty because he intentionally makes a false confession or forges other evidence of guilt;
(2) a person who, in accordance with Article 17 or Article 18 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China, does not bear criminal liability is placed in custody;
(3) a person who, in accordance with Article 15, paragraph 2 of Article 173, paragraph 2 of Article 273, or Article 279 of the Criminal Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China, is not investigated for criminal liability is placed in custody;
(4) a personal act of a functionary of an organ exercising functions and powers of investigation, prosecution and adjudication, or of a detention house or prison administration authority, which is not related to the exercise of his functions and powers;
(5) damage caused by an intentional act of a citizen such as self-inflicted injury or self-mutilation; or
(6) other circumstances provided for by law.

Article 34 Where the right to life and health of a citizen is infringed upon, the compensation money shall be calculated according to the following provisions:
(1) If bodily injury is caused, medical expenses, nursing expenses, and compensation for reduced income due to lost working time shall be paid. The daily compensation for reduced income shall be calculated on the basis of the average daily wage of employees in the previous year of the state, with the maximum amount not exceeding five times the average annual wage of employees in the previous year of the state;
(2) If partial or total loss of the ability to work is caused, medical expenses, nursing expenses, expenses for assistive devices for daily living, rehabilitation expenses, and other necessary expenses increased due to the disability and expenses necessary for continuing treatment, as well as disability compensation, shall be paid. The disability compensation shall be determined according to the degree of loss of ability to work and the disability grade provided by the state, with the maximum amount not exceeding twenty times the average annual wage of employees in the previous year of the state. If total loss of the ability to work is caused, living expenses shall also be paid to any person without the ability to work whom the victim supported;
(3) If death is caused, death compensation and funeral expenses shall be paid, the total amount being twenty times the average annual wage of employees in the previous year of the state. Living expenses shall also be paid to any person without the ability to work whom the deceased supported before death.
The living expenses specified in items (2) and (3) of the preceding paragraph shall be paid by reference to the local minimum subsistence guarantee standard. If the person supported is a minor, living expenses shall be paid until the person reaches the age of eighteen; for any other person without the ability to work, living expenses shall be paid until the person's death.

Article 36 Where the property rights of a citizen, legal person, or other organization are infringed upon and damage is caused, the matter shall be dealt with according to the following provisions:
(1) If a fine, penalty, recovery, confiscation of property, or illegal expropriation or requisition of property is imposed, the property shall be returned;
(2) If property is sealed up, seized, or frozen, the sealing, seizure, or freezing shall be lifted; if damage or loss is caused to the property, compensation shall be made in accordance with items (3) and (4) of this Article;
(3) If the property to be returned is damaged, the original condition shall be restored if possible; if restoration is not possible, corresponding compensation money shall be paid according to the extent of the damage;
(4) If the property to be returned is lost, corresponding compensation money shall be paid;
(5) If the property has been auctioned or sold off, the proceeds from the auction or sale shall be paid; if the proceeds from the sale are obviously lower than the value of the property, corresponding compensation money shall be paid;
(6) If a permit or license is revoked, or production or business operation is ordered to cease or suspend, the necessary recurrent expenses during the period of cessation or suspension shall be compensated;
(7) If a fine or penalty already executed is returned, or money recovered or confiscated is returned, or frozen deposits or remittances are unfrozen, interest on deposits at the bank for the same period shall be paid;
(8) If other damage is caused to property rights, compensation shall be given for direct losses.
